---
import Shot from '../components/Shot.astro';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { REPO } from '../data/site';
---
<Base
  title="Every mile, on the record."
  description="Axlebook is a free, self-hosted logbook for your vehicles: fuel economy, maintenance reminders, service records and costs, on your own server."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <svg class="gauge" viewBox="0 0 600 600" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
      <g fill="none" stroke="currentColor">
        <circle cx="300" cy="300" r="120" />
        <circle cx="300" cy="300" r="180" />
        <circle cx="300" cy="300" r="240" />
        <circle cx="300" cy="300" r="296" />
      </g>
      <path class="arc" d="M 130 470 A 240 240 0 1 1 470 470" fill="none" stroke-width="6" stroke-linecap="round" />
      <line class="needle" x1="300" y1="300" x2="420" y2="180" stroke-width="8" stroke-linecap="round" />
      <circle class="hub" cx="300" cy="300" r="12" />
    </svg>
    <div class="wrap hero-grid">
      <div>
        <img class="lockup" src="/brand/axlebook-lockup-horizontal-on-dark.svg" alt="Axlebook" width="440" height="96" />
        <h1 class="ax-display">Every mile, on the record.</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          A free, self-hosted logbook for your cars, bikes, sleds and semis: fuel, maintenance, reminders
          and costs, kept on your own server.
        </p>
        <div class="actions">
          <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/docs/#install">Get started</a>
          <a class="btn btn-ghost" href={REPO}>View on GitHub</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="panel" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="panel-head">
          <img src="/brand/axlebook-icon-default.svg" alt="" width="72" height="72" />
          <div>
            <p class="panel-title">2015 Toyota Tacoma</p>
            <p class="panel-sub mono">Demo data</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="panel-label">Odometer</p>
        <p class="readout mono">
          {['0', '8', '5', '9', '4'].map((d) => <span>{d}</span>)}<span class="last">2</span><small>mi</small>
        </p>
        <dl class="panel-stats">
          <div><dt>Average</dt><dd class="mono">19.7 mpg</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Oil change</dt><dd class="status"><span class="dot"></span>Overdue</dd></div>
        </dl>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap story" aria-labelledby="why">
    <h2 id="why">Why I made this</h2>
    <p>
      For years my truck’s history lived in three places: a spreadsheet I stopped updating, a shoebox of
      receipts, and a sticker in the corner of the windshield that was usually wrong. I wanted one place that
      knew when the oil was actually due, what the truck really gets per gallon, and what it has cost me since
      I bought it, without handing that to yet another app that wants an account and a subscription.
    </p>
    <p>
      Axlebook is that place. It runs on your own server or a Raspberry Pi in the closet, it doesn’t phone home,
      and your records never leave your network unless you send them somewhere.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap rows" aria-label="A closer look">
    <div class="row">
      <div class="row-text">
        <h2>Log it at the pump</h2>
        <p>
          The fill-up form remembers your vehicle and fills in today’s date. Type any two of gallons, price and
          total and it works out the third. No signal at the gas station? It keeps the entry on your phone and
          sends it when you’re back online.
        </p>
        <p>
          Economy is worked out full tank to full tank, so a partial fill carries into the next one and a
          fill-up you forgot to log only voids that stretch instead of dragging down the average.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="row-shot phone">
        <Shot name="phone-log" alt="Logging a fill-up on a phone" width={300} />
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row flip">
      <div class="row-text">
        <h2>The next oil change schedules itself</h2>
        <p>
          Reminders can be due by date, by miles, or whichever comes first. When you log the job, the next one
          is set from that record, not from the old due date, so a late oil change doesn’t make the next one
          early.
        </p>
        <p>
          Each vehicle also gets a maintenance schedule for its type, matched against what you’ve already logged,
          so you can see what’s overdue on a truck you’ve owned for years.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="row-shot">
        <Shot name="vehicle" alt="A vehicle’s overview: average economy, cost per mile, an overdue oil change and tips" width={720} />
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
      <div class="row-text">
        <h2>Bring the spreadsheet you already keep</h2>
        <p>
          Upload the .xlsx or .csv you’ve been keeping, even if it has a tab per vehicle or every vehicle in one
          sheet. Axlebook works out which column is which, what units you used and which vehicle each row is for,
          then shows you a preview before anything is saved. Import it twice and the second time skips what’s
          already there.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="row-shot">
        <Shot name="import" alt="Importing a workbook with a pickup and a snowmobile, previewed before saving" width={720} />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap also" aria-labelledby="also">
    <h2 id="also">Also in the box</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Service, repair, upgrade and expense records with receipts attached</li>
      <li>Motorcycles, dirt bikes, ATVs, snowmobiles, semis and trailers</li>
      <li>Engine-hour meters and electric vehicles</li>
      <li>Parts on a shelf, used up as you log jobs</li>
      <li>Reports by month and category, printable or as CSV</li>
      <li>Notifications by email, ntfy, Gotify, Discord or webhook</li>
      <li>Household accounts, sharing and single sign-on</li>
      <li>Inspections and an IFTA worksheet for owner-operators</li>
      <li>A calendar link for due dates</li>
      <li>A REST API with docs on your own server</li>
      <li>An optional local assistant (Ollama) that scans receipts and answers questions from your records</li>
    </ul>
    <p><a href="/features/">Everything it does, in more detail</a></p>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap own" aria-labelledby="yours">
    <div>
      <h2 id="yours">Your server, your data</h2>
      <p>
        No account to create, nothing to pay, and nothing sent anywhere you didn’t set up yourself. One button in
        Settings downloads a backup of every record, photo and receipt.
      </p>
    </div>
    <dl class="spec">
      <div><dt>Runs on</dt><dd>Docker, amd64 or arm64</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Database</dt><dd>SQLite, or Postgres</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Telemetry</dt><dd>None</dd></div>
      <div><dt>License</dt><dd>AGPL-3.0</dd></div>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap install" aria-labelledby="install">
    <h2 id="install">Running it</h2>
    <pre tabindex="0"><code>git clone https://github.com/aubergine-ux/axlebook.git
cd axlebook
docker compose up -d</code></pre>
    <p>
      Then open <code>http://localhost:8080</code> and create your account. The <a href="/docs/">docs</a> cover
      configuration, backups and reverse proxies. The code is <a href={REPO}>on GitHub</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .hero {
    /* Graphite in both themes, like the brand guide cover. */
    --focus: #ffab4a;
    position: relative;
    overflow: hidden;
    background:
      radial-gradient(40rem 28rem at 85% 20%, rgba(255, 138, 0, 0.12), transparent 70%),
      linear-gradient(180deg, #1c1f22, #121416);
    color: #f2f4f5;
    padding: 48px 0 56px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #2a2e33;
  }
  .gauge {
    position: absolute;
    width: 760px;
    max-width: none;
    right: -260px;
    top: -120px;
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.06);
    pointer-events: none;
  }
  /* On narrow screens the gauge sits behind the text: keep the faint arcs, drop the needle. */
  @media (max-width: 899px) {
    .gauge {
      right: -380px;
      top: -200px;
    }
    .gauge .needle,
    .gauge .hub {
      display: none;
    }
    .gauge .arc {
      opacity: 0.4;
    }
  }
  .gauge .arc {
    stroke: rgba(255, 154, 31, 0.35);
  }
  .gauge .needle {
    stroke: #ff9a1f;
  }
  .gauge .hub {
    fill: #ff9a1f;
  }
  .hero-grid {
    position: relative;
    display: grid;
    gap: 40px;
    align-items: center;
  }
  .lockup {
    width: 240px;
    height: auto;
    margin-bottom: 28px;
  }
  h1 {
    font-size: 40px;
    line-height: 1.05;
    margin-bottom: 16px;
    max-width: 16ch;
  }
  .hero .lede {
    color: #c4cad0;
    margin-bottom: 28px;
  }
  .btn-ghost {
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.06);
    border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.32);
    color: #f2f4f5;
  }
  .btn-ghost:hover {
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.12);
  }
  .panel {
    justify-self: start;
    width: min(100%, 380px);
    padding: 22px;
    border-radius: var(--radius-xl);
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.06);
    border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.12);
    -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(20px) saturate(150%);
    backdrop-filter: blur(20px) saturate(150%);
    box-shadow:
      inset 0 1px 0 rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.16),
      0 24px 48px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.35);
  }
  .panel p {
    margin: 0;
  }
  .panel-head {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 14px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
  }
  .panel-title {
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  .panel-sub,
  .panel-label,
  dt {
    color: #a3aab1;
    font-size: 14px;
  }
  .readout {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-end;
    gap: 5px;
    margin: 6px 0 20px !important;
  }
  .readout span {
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    width: 40px;
    height: 52px;
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    background: #2c3136;
    color: #f2f4f5;
    font-size: 30px;
    font-weight: 600;
    box-shadow: inset 0 1px 0 rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08);
  }
  .readout .last {
    background: #ff9a1f;
    color: #1a1206;
  }
  .readout small {
    margin-left: 4px;
    color: #a3aab1;
    font-size: 16px;
  }
  .panel-stats {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 12px;
    margin: 0;
    padding-top: 16px;
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);
  }
  dd {
    margin: 2px 0 0;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .status {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 6px;
    color: #ff857a;
  }
  .dot {
    width: 8px;
    height: 8px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: #ff857a;
  }
  @media (min-width: 900px) {
    .hero {
      padding: 88px 0 96px;
    }
    .hero-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1.3fr 1fr;
    }
    .panel {
      justify-self: end;
    }
    h1 {
      font-size: 64px;
    }
    .lockup {
      width: 320px;
    }
  }
  .story p,
  .install p {
    max-width: 62ch;
  }
  .story {
    padding-top: 64px;
    padding-bottom: 24px;
    font-size: 19px;
  }
  .rows {
    padding-top: 24px;
  }
  .row {
    display: grid;
    gap: 28px;
    align-items: center;
    padding: 48px 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .row-text {
    max-width: 52ch;
  }
  .row-text p {
    color: var(--ink-muted);
  }
  .phone {
    max-width: 300px;
  }
  @media (min-width: 900px) {
    .row {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1.35fr;
      gap: 56px;
    }
    .row.flip {
      grid-template-columns: 1.35fr 1fr;
    }
    .row.flip .row-text {
      order: 2;
    }
    .row:first-child {
      grid-template-columns: 1.4fr 1fr;
    }
    .phone {
      justify-self: center;
    }
  }
  .also {
    padding-top: 48px;
    padding-bottom: 24px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .also ul {
    columns: 2 300px;
    column-gap: 48px;
    padding-left: 1.1em;
    margin: 0 0 20px;
  }
  .also li {
    margin: 0 0 8px;
    break-inside: avoid;
  }
  .own {
    display: grid;
    gap: 24px;
    padding-top: 48px;
    padding-bottom: 24px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  @media (min-width: 900px) {
    .own {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
      gap: 56px;
    }
  }
  .spec {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 15px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line-strong);
  }
  .spec div {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 16px;
    padding: 10px 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .spec dt {
    color: var(--ink-muted);
  }
  .spec dd {
    margin: 0;
    text-align: right;
  }
  .install {
    padding-top: 48px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .install pre {
    max-width: 640px;
  }
</style>
